		<div id="text-186502524" class="p">
			
		 	
				Binance is <a href="https://x.com/binance/status/2115915483832832425?s=46">investigating</a> a potential hack after <a href="https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/29/potential-multi-billion-binance-hack-hitting-crypto-markets">more than $2 billion in crypto was drained from one of its wallets</a> into a new external account, with Blockaid <a href="https://x.com/blockaid_/status/2115914335512150480">estimating</a> nearly $3.3 billion was moved.
<br> <br>
"Our teams are aware of reports of a potential security issue and are actively investigating," <a href="https://x.com/binance/status/2115915483832832425?s=46">said</a> Binance on X.
<br> <br>
"User funds are safe," <a href="https://x.com/cz_binance/status/2115915423174853077">said</a> Binance founder CZ. "It does look like a hack on Binance. Appreciate the quick freeze from Tether (~$971m) and Circle (~$823m). I don't manage Binance anymore, but as a shareholder, I expect all user funds will be fully covered."<br>
		 	
