<div class="body" id="fhbody-186492092">
	

	
		
		<div id="text-186492092" class="p">
			
		 	
				Reddit is overhauling its homepage with <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1020751/reddit-for-you-following-feeds">separate "For You" and "Following" feeds</a>, with the former combining posts from subscribed communities and algorithmic recommendations based on users' interests and activity. The Verge reports: <i> It's a big shift for the platform, but not an entirely surprising one, as Reddit hasn't been shy about wanting to switch up the homepage. Earlier this year, the company announced it would be deprecating r/all, which surfaced posts that were popular across the platform, as part of its "ongoing efforts to simplify Reddit and improve Home feed personalization." </i> "This new feed experience is a first step in helping drive discovery that leads to something novel and relevant -- an idea, a connection, a unique perspective, or even a new interest," Reddit <a href="https://redditinc.com/news/explore-more-communities-with-reddits-new-feed-updates">says</a>. "A more human internet is not just something you sit back and watch, it is something you find value in and want to participate in."<br>
		 	
		</div>

		

		

		
	</div>
