<div class="body" id="fhbody-186487338">
	

	
		
		<div id="text-186487338" class="p">
			
		 	
				Amazon has <a href="https://thenextweb.com/news/amazon-echo-studio-camera-echo-dot-show-16-alexa-devices">added a camera to its Echo Studio speaker</a>, allowing Alexa to visually identify objects, help with tasks and remotely monitor a room. For those concerned about privacy, Amazon is keeping a camera-free version available. The Next Web reports: <i> The camera speaker ships today for $249.99. Hold up a board game box and Alexa can explain the rules, or show it a box of cereal and it can help you reorder it, <a href="https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/devices/echo-speaker-lineup">according to Amazon</a>. Owners can also check in on the room from the Alexa app while they are away. The Echo Studio without a camera stays on sale at $219.99.
